hi,

i've just uploaded a fresh binary bundle of the most recent development 
snapshot of RKWard for OS X:
 http://sourceforge.net/projects/rkwardextras/files/MacOSX/development/RKWard-devel-binary-0.6.1-svn4755_KDE-4.10.3_needs_CRAN_R-3.0.0.dmg

its main purpose is to let you test the new graphics device, which is supposed 
to become one of the main new features of the next release. for the first time 
it enables all graphics features of RKWard (like plot history, easy export 
etc.) for mac users.

as the file name suggests, it's supposed to be installed *after* R from CRAN 
was installed (>= 3.0.0). if you want to test the package, follow the 
"UPDATES/UNINSTALL" instructions in the README to replace an earlier version.

and of course, we're interested in your feedback on what's great and what 
isn't. since it's bleeding endge, it's totally possible it doesn't work for 
you at all, so you shouldn't try this on productive machines.


